1
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:17,400
Those who ceaselessly hone the art
of killing are known as masters.

2
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:22,037
These lethal abilities, dutifully
passed down through many generations,

3
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:25,120
have become what are
called modified bloodlines.

4
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:28,757
This is the story of one such master,

5
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:32,640
Hikaru Gero of the Poison Clan
and his greatest challenge yet,

6
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:34,080
to get married.

7
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:57,260
No mama, lots of time?

8
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,120
Let's go!

9
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:54,320
Kill a kiss, can't kill a kiss!

10
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,660
Kill a kiss, can't kill a kiss!

11
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:01,340
Kill a kiss, can't kill a kiss!

12
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:07,130
Cheers!

13
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:17,300
Thank you for being so patient.

14
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:19,193
Got those sours for ya.

15
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:23,140
I hope Gero's up for this.

16
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:28,840
So this is a college welcome party.

17
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:30,413
I've heard the legends.

18
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:33,340
I never thought my job would take me here.

19
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:35,660
New students! Move in!

20
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:44,817
Let's hear it for all of us starting
college and meeting for the first time.

21
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:46,180
Cheers! Cheers!

22
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:54,128
You're a first year, right?

23
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,988
Is the party getting
you excited for school?

24
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:11,030
Yeah.

25
00:03:11,113 --> 00:03:12,940
I'm having tons of fun over here.

26
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:14,620
What did we say?

27
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,273
We're just going to go.

28
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:17,840
Yeah, see you around.

29
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:25,320
This is my chance to talk to
upperclassmen and I blew it.

30
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:33,580
I want to hire you as a bodyguard for my
niece who starts university this spring.

31
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:36,540
If possible, be discreet.

32
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:38,530
I...

33
00:03:38,613 --> 00:03:39,460
don't stand out!

34
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:41,980
I'm Shiori Ureshino.

35
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:44,720
Her father was my older brother.

36
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:48,805
He built this company from the
ground up in a single generation.

37
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:51,891
He passed away from an illness a year ago.

38
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:54,954
But according to the terms of his will,

39
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:59,500
Shiori will succeed him as
CEO once she comes of age.

40
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:05,304
However, there are some who didn't
agree with his final decision.

41
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,820
My older sister, for one.

42
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:10,437
She claims Balzac is rightfully hers.

43
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:11,920
No question about it.

44
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:13,780
Cards on the table?

45
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:15,457
I don't know what she'll attempt.

46
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:19,140
But rumor is, she's gone and
hired a professional herself.

47
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:23,424
Someone with strange techniques
that no ordinary expert can stop.

48
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:26,080
I'm grateful.

49
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,477
I need help.

50
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:29,340
So thanks for taking the job.

51
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:32,600
Your student ID. Don't lose it.

52
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:36,057
Starting today, you're
Daigo Oshima, a third year.

53
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:37,199
You're kidding me.

54
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:39,500
Sorry, ma 'am.

55
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:43,180
This is sudden, but could we maybe...

56
00:04:45,260 --> 00:04:49,000
If it's possible, go to drinking party?

57
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:52,285
Sorry, but that's a risk
we don't need to take.

58
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:53,980
Please, can I go?

59
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:01,700
Okay, only this once, though.

60
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:08,260
Okay, who's up next?

61
00:05:09,980 --> 00:05:12,900
I'm Shiori Ureshino,

62
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:19,800
a first-year economics
major, and I like...

63
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:26,620
I did it again.

64
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:27,900
What should I say?

65
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,365
You're the Tokugawa shogunaga.

66
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:35,717
Part of the lore.

67
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:36,800
Back to the lore.

68
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:39,977
I am

69
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:46,740
pleased to meet you.

70
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:49,250
Huh.

71
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:51,772
Well, thanks a lot for that introduction.

72
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,400
Okay, next person.

73
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,420
Can you handle a party, Gato?

74
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:04,120
I've had drinks with the
Bug Master loads of times.

75
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:05,894
You've got me worried.

76
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:07,276
I'd better sneak in.

77
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:09,270
You'll see.

78
00:06:09,353 --> 00:06:11,240
I'm not just a master assassin.

79
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:13,600
I'm also the life of the party.

80
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:17,000
Name's Oshima. Econ Major.

81
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:20,620
Now observe as I chug eight pints at once.

82
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:25,640
What is this, a 90s movie?

83
00:06:31,780 --> 00:06:33,800
Now for the grand finale.

84
00:06:41,060 --> 00:06:43,531
We should call an ambulance, shouldn't we?

85
00:06:58,420 --> 00:06:59,940
Here comes the applause.

86
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:03,160
Great to meet you all.

87
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:06,924
It's a water-absorbent polymer!

88
00:07:07,140 --> 00:07:08,611
It's completely harmless!

89
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:10,480
That's nasty.

90
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:14,906
Anybody else who hasn't
introduced themselves?

91
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:16,376
Hey, man, you're up.

92
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:18,190
Hmm.

93
00:07:30,420 --> 00:07:31,560
My name's Naruko.

94
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:34,510
That's all.

95
00:07:35,140 --> 00:07:37,480
How about your first name? Your major?

96
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:38,697
You know, stuff like that.

97
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:39,898
That's unimportant.

98
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:41,150
Huh?

99
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:44,557
The only thing that truly
matters is that I was

100
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:47,934
fortunate enough to meet all
of you here in this moment.

101
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:50,880
For that, I thank my lucky stars.

102
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,161
What's his deal?

103
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:54,576
He's been spaced out this whole time.

104
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:57,040
Super thank them.

105
00:07:58,380 --> 00:07:59,737
That had no substance.

106
00:07:59,820 --> 00:08:01,467
And why did he say it twice?

107
00:08:01,820 --> 00:08:03,940
I searched for you. My true love.

108
00:08:06,620 --> 00:08:08,149
Naruko, is the seat taken?

109
00:08:08,340 --> 00:08:09,170
Do you mind if I say over here?

110
00:08:09,253 --> 00:08:11,857
How come I can't make a first
impression as good as this weirdo?

111
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:13,352
It's gotta be his books.

112
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:17,580
These drinking parties, it
appears they have hidden depths.

113
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:22,620
Is this all?

114
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:26,380
Listen, Ureshino.

115
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:27,950
I'm sorry!

116
00:08:28,033 --> 00:08:30,717
Don't lash out at her
because you're trick-bombed.

117
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:32,297
I swear, if you make her cry...

118
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:33,220
What? Come on!

119
00:08:33,340 --> 00:08:34,634
I didn't say anything!

120
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:39,897
I just don't understand why you're
forcing yourself to go to these.

121
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:43,837
I get you're inheriting a company and
trying to overcome your social anxiety,

122
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:46,155
but there's no need to force yourself.

123
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:50,390
Huh?

124
00:08:50,473 --> 00:08:51,303
What did I say?

125
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:52,282
Really, Ghetto?

126
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:56,040
No, I'm not sad.

127
00:08:56,520 --> 00:08:57,580
Just overwhelmed.

128
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:59,329
You care about how I feel.

129
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:04,780
The truth is, it's not about the company.

130
00:09:05,560 --> 00:09:09,100
What I want is to be able to
fit in with everyone else.

131
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:16,680
When my dad reached the
end, he said to me...

132
00:09:20,140 --> 00:09:22,120
You should give drinking a try.

133
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:25,560
But be sure to wait until you're twenty.

134
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:32,900
My Shiori, you're a
nice girl, I mean that.

135
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:36,398
But you worry too much about
what other people think.

136
00:09:38,220 --> 00:09:43,377
Trust me, you've got to take everything
that's pent up inside and bam,

137
00:09:43,460 --> 00:09:45,520
let it all out like a firework.

138
00:09:45,900 --> 00:09:50,180
Enjoy life and the time
you have with others.

139
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,160
above all else.

140
00:09:52,820 --> 00:09:54,600
I want that for you.

141
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:07,820
I can't do it.

142
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:09,800
Even here with you.

143
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:13,700
I still freeze up and the
words refuse to come up.

144
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:15,500
It takes time.

145
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:16,657
I know it.

146
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:17,797
You don't have to say it.

147
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:20,097
The hardest part is taking the first step.

148
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:22,500
After that, everyone will accept me.

149
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:25,660
But I can't help worrying.

150
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:29,437
What if they get sick of me
the moment I open my mouth?

151
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:32,140
What if I annoy them or make them angry?

152
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:38,832
There was still time when I didn't even
have the courage to talk to my dad.

153
00:10:39,980 --> 00:10:42,568
Never know why he named
me as his successor.

154
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:45,060
And not someone else.

155
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:50,100
That's why I want to improve myself.

156
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:54,617
To face the things that scare me so one

157
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:59,437
day I could laugh away fear you know.

158
00:10:59,520 --> 00:11:05,317
Someone's out to kill you right oh but if

159
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:07,457
you want to go somewhere I won't stop you.

160
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:13,260
My job is keeping you safe and
nothing will get in my way.

161
00:11:18,140 --> 00:11:20,097
Madame, I have your report.

162
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:23,097
Her bodyguard is good.

163
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:26,077
Well, he might act laid back.

164
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:28,420
He leaves no openings.

165
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:37,160
I super forgot to charge my phone.

166
00:11:42,220 --> 00:11:45,497
Is this a game to you
I've given you an entire

167
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:47,837
month and you've made
zero progress what am I?

168
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:50,677
paying you for a party supply company with

169
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:53,597
a market cap of 1.5
trillion yen is at stake

170
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:56,437
As if that meek little
girl is fit to take over

171
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:59,680
so tell me how long
until you dispose of her?

172
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:04,537
Hmm, in a while, when it's right!

173
00:12:04,620 --> 00:12:07,797
Excuse me, don't give me
this when I'm ready, crap!

174
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:09,060
I'm paying you to!

175
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:19,240
This bodyguard, Oshima!

176
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:22,337
You say he's good, but
he's still a nobody!

177
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:25,620
And wouldn't last a second
against a master like you!

178
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:29,460
Madam, I'm a man of my word!

179
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:31,700
In any case,

180
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:34,817
either convince that brat to renounce her

181
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:38,660
inheritance or leave her
unfit to inherit anything.

182
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:42,560
If killing her is what it
takes, then by all means.

183
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:48,370
Gato,

184
00:12:48,453 --> 00:12:52,237
you realize you're not a real student
and don't have to listen to the lectures.

185
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:54,357
I've never been in a classroom before.

186
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,320
This is fun.

187
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:57,640
That backstory is hella tragic.

188
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:00,097
One more day.

189
00:13:00,180 --> 00:13:01,977
You there, in the hoodie.

190
00:13:02,060 --> 00:13:04,880
Name a product that
transformed its industry?

191
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:08,137
Mixy mix, max mix.

192
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:11,737
A hundred of these kits were made
for the brand's 30th anniversary.

193
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:13,657
It's Candy's holy grail.

194
00:13:13,740 --> 00:13:14,917
Not bad.

195
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,882
Looks like at least one
of you knows their stuff?

196
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,040
It renewed the Mixi-Mix market!

197
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:49,060
A return to the Mix-a-sance!

198
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:52,000
Because of Mixi-Mix Max-Mix! Fact!

199
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:56,237
As long as there are
passionate students like you,

200
00:13:56,320 --> 00:14:00,026
I could retire and leave things
in the next generation's hands.

201
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:05,140
I should have known.

202
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:09,577
Since they can't separate me from the
target, they're using brute force.

203
00:14:09,660 --> 00:14:11,189
Who here looks suspicious?

204
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:16,340
They're outside.

205
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:20,409
I already made sure no one had
line of sight into this room.

206
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,588
That attack affected
the whole lecture hall.

207
00:14:43,860 --> 00:14:48,540
However, this is a well-ventilated
environment, ruling out a gas attack.

208
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:51,617
Which would mean...

209
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:55,229
He injected himself with something
that allowed him to move.

210
00:14:56,320 --> 00:15:00,460
Sound waves transmitted remotely,
to shake the room and its occupants.

211
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:03,177
His equilibrium should
have been scrambled,

212
00:15:03,260 --> 00:15:06,340
but somehow he's
super-recovered in no time flat.

213
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:10,577
No one could pull off such a precise,
large-scale attack, except...

214
00:15:10,660 --> 00:15:14,954
There's only one person who could
produce a cure like that in an instant.

215
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:16,980
A poison master.

216
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:22,270
Ghetto!

217
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:25,228
The client's been informed.

218
00:15:25,620 --> 00:15:27,857
Making it look like an
accident saves trouble.

219
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:29,040
That's Hitman 101.

220
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:32,530
Ureshino.

221
00:15:32,613 --> 00:15:35,046
Clearly, their intention
was to eliminate you.

222
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:36,860
What's the plan?

223
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:39,456
Do we skip the camping trip tomorrow?

224
00:15:39,920 --> 00:15:41,332
That's up to our client.

225
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:44,220
Of course you can go.

226
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:46,820
Really? I can?

227
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:48,350
Absolutely.

228
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:51,877
You've been looking forward
to this trip for ages, right?

229
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:55,666
There's no substitute for the
fringe you'll make at university.

230
00:15:56,460 --> 00:15:58,000
Meet as many as you can.

231
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:02,106
Besides, with those two around,
there's nothing to worry about.

232
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:04,860
Good morning.

233
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:07,660
Uncle Mitsuki, I'm leaving.

234
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:10,389
Sorry to keep you waiting.

235
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:11,690
No worries.

236
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:13,757
That's kind of a huge bag, though.

237
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:14,899
What did you pack?

238
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:17,057
A collapsible umbrella.

239
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:18,037
Have a safe trip.

240
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:19,826
Actually, the rest is secret.

241
00:16:25,260 --> 00:16:29,025
Even if she stayed home, there's
no way to guarantee her safety.

242
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:32,181
The only way to end this
is confronting the enemy.

243
00:16:33,780 --> 00:16:38,074
And unlike with Himekawa, we don't
know when the Soundmaster will strike.

244
00:16:39,780 --> 00:16:42,251
Is the plan to settle things on this trip?

245
00:16:48,660 --> 00:16:50,360
Hey, what does this mean?

246
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:53,160
An important promise I can't bring.

247
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:54,997
You're so thoughtful, Maruko.

248
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:57,057
I've got a promise I want to make you.

249
00:16:57,140 --> 00:17:00,377
How about you make one with me
first, since I'm closer than her?

250
00:17:00,460 --> 00:17:01,290
There, we can't!

251
00:17:01,373 --> 00:17:02,640
It's super important.

252
00:17:20,360 --> 00:17:23,780
A man who can cook is three
times hotter to the ladies.

253
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:26,689
Time to unleash those
skills on the public.

254
00:17:29,460 --> 00:17:32,401
I'll show you I can compete
with the best of them.

255
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:35,240
Yakisoba, I made it myself.

256
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:37,440
Want to try some?

257
00:17:39,340 --> 00:17:40,170
Anyone?

258
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:42,040
It's delicious.

259
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:44,750
Yakisoba.

260
00:17:46,700 --> 00:17:47,897
Should we step in?

261
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:50,500
Have fun and don't worry about me.

262
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:54,220
That's what Ureshino told us, remember?

